toiimg.com/photo/msid-133717167,imgsize-829693.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[China's Xi tells Middle East to be ‘masters of their own destiny’ amid Iran war]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133716224.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Chinese President Xi Jinping urged Middle Eastern nations to resist external interference.  He called for reshaping the region's security order during talks with Egypt's President Sisi.  Both leaders agreed to deepen security and economic cooperation between their nations.  China seeks to expand its influence and safeguard vital shipping routes.  Egypt is diversifying its international partnerships by strengthening ties with Beijing.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/china/chinas-xi-jinping-tells-middle-east-to-be-masters-of-their-own-destiny-amid-iran-war/articleshow/133716224.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/china/chinas-xi-jinping-tells-middle-east-to-be-masters-of-their-own-destiny-amid-iran-war/articleshow/133716224.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-02T22:39:52+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133716589,imgsize-80362.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[After their brother died, two siblings inherited 20.66 acres beside Zion National Park]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133691288.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a heartfelt tribute to their late brother, two siblings have secured twenty-point-six-six acres of pristine land bordering Zion National Park through a conservation easement with the Virgin River Land Conservancy. This commitment ensures that the land remains untouched by commercial development, serving as a refuge for wildlife and offering breathtaking views of the iconic red sandstone formations, reinforcing their dedication to environmental stewardship.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/after-their-brother-died-two-siblings-inherited-20-66-acres-beside-zion-national-park-they-gave-up-development-rights-so-it-can-never-be-built-on/articleshow/133691288.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/after-their-brother-died-two-siblings-inherited-20-66-acres-beside-zion-national-park-they-gave-up-development-rights-so-it-can-never-be-built-on/articleshow/133691288.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-03T03:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133691336,imgsize-2565521.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Scientists removed 285,000 fish from a Wisconsin lake to help walleye, but perch rose 788% instead]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133706721.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Scientists removed about 285,000 centrarchid fish from Wisconsin’s McDermott Lake between 2018 and 2021 to see if reducing competition and predation could help walleye recover. The experiment sharply reduced several fish species and saw yellow perch numbers rise by about 788%. However, researchers found no detectable natural walleye recruitment, showing that removing centrarchids alone did not restore the lake’s walleye population.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-2018-scientists-began-removing-about-285000-fish-from-wisconsins-mcdermott-lake-4-years-later-yellow-perch-were-up-788-but-walleye-recruitment-was-still-zero/articleshow/133706721.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-2018-scientists-began-removing-about-285000-fish-from-wisconsins-mcdermott-lake-4-years-later-yellow-perch-were-up-788-but-walleye-recruitment-was-still-zero/articleshow/133706721.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-03T02:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133708822,imgsize-84378.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Wisconsin family’s 2,000 floodplain acres protected after decade-long fight]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133707338.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-wisconsin-farming-family-fought-a-2016-tax-change-as-nearly-2000-floodplain-acres-became-harder-to-farm-10-years-later-the-land-is-being-permanently-protected/articleshow/133707338.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-wisconsin-farming-family-fought-a-2016-tax-change-as-nearly-2000-floodplain-acres-became-harder-to-farm-10-years-later-the-land-is-being-permanently-protected/articleshow/133707338.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-03T01:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133707602,imgsize-148087.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[California could unlock $100M-$200M in annual water value by using better forecasts at 20 reservoirs]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133706508.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[To boost water availability in California, advanced weather forecast models can play a crucial role. Implementing Forecast-Informed Reservoir Operations may yield an additional 315,000 acre-feet each year, providing substantial economic leverage for both farmers and city dwellers. This innovative approach improves flood management and opens up opportunities for environmental flow, all while promoting conservation and aiding in infrastructure advancements.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/a-california-reservoir-forecasting-system-could-add-enough-usable-water-to-save-100-million-to-200-million-a-year-without-building-a-new-reservoir-a-study-estimates/articleshow/133706508.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/a-california-reservoir-forecasting-system-could-add-enough-usable-water-to-save-100-million-to-200-million-a-year-without-building-a-new-reservoir-a-study-estimates/articleshow/133706508.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-03T00:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133706855,imgsize-1928531.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 1947, Houston opened a 700-seat Art Deco theater; 79 years later, $2.8M was raised to save it]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133704241.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Houston's historic Garden Oaks Theater faced demolition after its sale in 2025. A local preservation campaign successfully raised funds to acquire the property. The nonprofit Arthouse Houston plans to transform the building into an arts and film center. This new center will combine historic preservation with new cultural uses. The completed center is targeted for a grand opening in 2028.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1947-houston-opened-a-700-plus-seat-art-deco-theater-79-years-later-after-demolition-was-planned-supporters-raised-2-8-million-toward-saving-the-7-1-million-property/articleshow/133704241.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1947-houston-opened-a-700-plus-seat-art-deco-theater-79-years-later-after-demolition-was-planned-supporters-raised-2-8-million-toward-saving-the-7-1-million-property/articleshow/133704241.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-02T23:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133704669,imgsize-1290116.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Meet the 18-year-old whose junk hauling business earns up to $15,000 a month]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133688146.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-carter-grandbois-the-18-year-old-who-started-hauling-junk-at-16-his-colorado-business-now-bills-up-to-15000-a-month/articleshow/133688146.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-carter-grandbois-the-18-year-old-who-started-hauling-junk-at-16-his-colorado-business-now-bills-up-to-15000-a-month/articleshow/133688146.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-02T23:51:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133688390,imgsize-141854.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[California condo owners were suddenly handed a $26,000 HOA bill each]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133691190.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Residents of Vilamoura are grappling with an unanticipated $26,000 emergency roof assessment mandated by their HOA, causing considerable distress, especially among the retirees living on fixed incomes. Many homeowners argue that the board has neglected crucial repairs for far too long and are now taking legal action, as well as initiating recall measures against the board. To cover legal expenses and assist neighbors in need, a GoFundMe has been launched.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/california-condo-owners-were-suddenly-handed-a-26000-hoa-bill-each-an-81-year-old-resident-says-she-may-have-to-leave-the-home-she-worked-hard-to-keep/articleshow/133691190.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/california-condo-owners-were-suddenly-handed-a-26000-hoa-bill-each-an-81-year-old-resident-says-she-may-have-to-leave-the-home-she-worked-hard-to-keep/articleshow/133691190.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-02T22:53:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133691275,imgsize-1677751.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Princess Diana's godson Prince Philippos and Princess Nina welcome first child via surrogate]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133716195.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Princess Diana’s godson, Prince Philippos of Greece, and Princess Nina have welcomed their first child, a son named Kimon Thomas Konstantinos. Born via surrogate in the United States on July 27, the baby’s arrival was announced weeks later. His middle names honour Nina’s father Thomas Flohr and Philippos’ late father, Constantine II, Greece’s last king.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/princess-dianas-godson-prince-philippos-and-princess-nina-welcome-first-child-son-kimon-thomas-konstantinos-via-surrogate-in-the-us-nearly-six-years-after-their-wedding/articleshow/133716195.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/princess-dianas-godson-prince-philippos-and-princess-nina-welcome-first-child-son-kimon-thomas-